THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Chromium bundles several hundred third-party components under their own
licences. The complete, per-component inventory is generated from the source
tree at build time and is available INSIDE THE BROWSER at:

    about:credits

That page is how the BSD-3-Clause notice requirement is met for binary
distribution, so it is never removed, never disabled, and is linked from the
About dialog.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS BUILD DOES NOT DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The ungoogled-chromium patches remove Chromium's integration with Google
services: no Safe Browsing callbacks, no component updater, no field trials,
no usage or crash reporting, and no Google API keys. Nothing contacts a
QuickOpen server either. The browser makes network connections when you ask it
to load a page, and otherwise stays quiet.

This build ships FREE CODECS ONLY -- VP8, VP9, AV1 and Opus. H.264 and AAC are
deliberately absent: the code is open but the formats are patent-encumbered,
and QuickOpen holds no patent licence for them. Some video on the web will not
play as a result. That is a considered trade, not an oversight.

